# Outward read-modify-write of a module global that a LATER statement demotes
# off the numeric class — the first silent-wrong compiler find in 12 rounds,
# surfaced by a sweep into territory the fuzzer is structurally blind to (its
# generators emit no outward writes, no demotion, no `local`).
#
# `v is "str"` at the END demotes module v to env-resident storage. The
# function-body classification recognized only numeric (gnm) and buffer (gbt)
# globals, so the body's outward `v is v + k` got a fresh zeroed C local:
#
#   bump of 2:   VM 3, AOT 2      and the module v never moved (VM 3, AOT 1)
#   both rc 0, silent, inside the claimed envelope
#
# The rule: a module-bound name assigned WITHOUT a `local` marker is an
# outward write whatever the binding's class — no body decl, no numeric
# promotion; reads take env_read_num, writes take the terminal env arm.
# A `local`-marked name stays a true body local (the last case below).

v is 1

define bump(k) as:
    v is v + k
    return v

print of (bump of 2)
x is bump of 2
print of v

v is "str"
print of v

w is 1

define shadowed(k) as:
    # `local` marker: a TRUE body local; module w must not move
    local w is 10
    w is w + k
    return w

print of (shadowed of 2)
print of w
w is "demoted-too"
print of w
